nghttp2 is a C implementation of the HTTP/2 framing layer (RFC 7540 / RFC 9113).
The library provides a session-oriented, callback-driven API for encoding and
decoding HTTP/2 frames, HPACK header compression, and flow-control accounting.
It performs no I/O itself — all network operations are delegated to the caller
via send/receive callbacks, making it well-suited for embedded targets.

This KOS port builds the core library only (lib/), with no external dependencies
beyond the standard C library. It is used by cURL to enable HTTP/2 multiplexing
over the Dreamcast's Broadband Adapter or modem connection.

URL: https://nghttp2.org
